          "status": "completed_http200_stop",
          "full_final": "Based on the analysis of the cube net:\n\n1.  We can determine the opposite faces by imagining the folding of the net. Let's keep the face labeled **V** as the stationary **Front** face.\n2.  The face **X** is directly below V, so it folds to become the **Bottom** face.\n3.  The face **W** is directly to the right of V, so it folds to become the **Right** face.\n4.  The face **Y** is above W. When W folds to the Right, Y folds over to become the **Top** face.\n5.  The face **U** is to the left of V, so it folds to become the **Left** face.\n6.  The face **Z** is below X. Since X is the Bottom face, Z folds up from the bottom to become the **Back** face.\n\nIn a cube, the Front face is opposite the Back face. Since V is the Front face and Z is the Back face, they are opposite each other.\n\nTherefore, the label of the face opposite the face labeled X is not directly asked (X is opposite Y), but the question asks to identify the opposite pair, which implies finding the face opposite the Front face V. The opposite of V is Z.\n\nThe correct choice is **A: Z**."
        },
